From 601ff4f2c2318428a5982d733f245d08749017e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:30:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(zh): merge Chinese card art and card text into ONE
 localization series
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

They were two series and could not be stacked. Every reason came down to the same
thing: the split was artificial. Both halves write the SAME files —
`preferencesStore.ts`, `PreferencesModal.tsx`, and the `settings.json` catalogs —
so as separate series each carried half a change to a shared file and they
conflicted no matter which order they were applied in.

They are one feature: "the game is in Chinese". Card art and card text are two
surfaces of it, not two capabilities, and the player reaches both through one
control (the interface language, which `artLanguage: "auto"` follows). One series,
one application, no conflict.

This is the engine base plus the localization content, so applying it produces a
complete Chinese install. The engine support remains its own series and is applied
first; only `client/` and the card-text generator are touched here.
